WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.470
Astronomers measure the
light from distant galaxies.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.390
Almost every one of them
is moving away from us.

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:11.270
And the further away a galaxy
is, the faster it is rushing off.

4
00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:14.550
Look in any direction,
and it's the same story.

5
00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.790
It is as if everything
is fleeing from us.

6
00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:21.210
Does that mean we are at
the centre of the universe?

7
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:24.790
In this mission, you'll see how
light from distant galaxies is

8
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.470
stretched, giving red-shift,

9
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:29.530
and what that tells us
about how they are moving.

10
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.170
You'll find out why this is
evidence for an expanding universe,

11
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.670
and for the Big Bang.

12
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.370
Your mission: decide whether we
really are at the centre of the

13
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.580
universe.
